Feature: Create and populate the sample_sales_data table in Unity Catalog

  Background:
    Given A Unity Catalog schema named "purgo_playground" exists

  Scenario: Successfully create and populate the sample_sales_data table
    When The table "sample_sales_data" is created in the "purgo_playground" schema with columns "country_cd" (string), "product_id" (string), "qty_sold" (int), and "sales_date" (date)
    And The following data is loaded into the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table:
      | country_cd | product_id | qty_sold | sales_date |
      | US         | P1001      | 50       | 2024-01-15 |
      | US         | P1002      | 30       | 2024-01-16 |
      | CA         | P1001      | 40       | 2024-01-15 |
      | CA         | P1003      | 25       | 2024-01-17 |
      | UK         | P1002      | 35       | 2024-01-18 |
      | UK         | P1004      | 20       | 2024-01-19 |
      | IN         | P1001      | 60       | 2024-01-20 |
      | IN         | P1003      | 45       | 2024-01-21 |
      | AU         | P1004      | 55       | 2024-01-22 |
      | AU         | P1002      | 38       | 2024-01-23 |
    Then The "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table should exist
    And The "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table should have 10 rows

  Scenario Outline: Validate data types in sample_sales_data table
    When The table "sample_sales_data" exists in the "purgo_playground" schema
    Then The column "<column_name>" in the "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data" table should have data type "<data_type>"

    Examples:
      | column_name | data_type |
      | country_cd  | string    |
      | product_id  | string    |
      | qty_sold    | int       |
      | sales_date  | date      |


  Scenario: Attempt to create the table with an invalid schema
    When The table "sample_sales_data" is created in the "purgo_playground" schema with an invalid schema
    Then The table creation should fail with an error message

  Scenario: Attempt to load data with incorrect data types
    When The table "sample_sales_data" exists in the "purgo_playground" schema
    And Attempting to load data with incorrect data types into "purgo_playground.sample_sales_data"
    Then The data load should fail with an error message